Given proposition $P$: $\forall x > 0$, $x + \frac{1}{x} \geqslant 2$.  
Consider the following four propositions:  

- Proposition $q_{1}$: $\forall x > 0$, $x^{2} + \frac{1}{x^{2}} \geqslant 2$;  
- Proposition $q_{2}$: $\forall x > 0$, $x^{2} + \frac{1}{x^{2}} \geqslant 4$;  
- Proposition $q_{3}$: $\forall x < 0$, $x + \frac{1}{x} \geqslant 2$;  
- Proposition $q_{4}$: $\exists x < 0$, $x + \frac{1}{x} < -2$.
